        "text": "We may describe blockchain as a trustless system. What are the implications of a distributed network which revolves around a single source of truth? It means security and redundancy. A blockchain can have tens of thousands of users, each storing their own copy and talking with peers. Even if many go offline, the network will continue to function. It also means immutability. Once a block is added to the blockchain, it can be considered permanent. It means trustlessness and transparency. You don't need to trust a anyone, and since everyone has a copy of the blockchain, they can see and verify all of the data it holds.",
